   173	## 5. A8.4's query (C-Q6k): the standing key is the key the innermost acceptance verified under
   174	
   175	**Where the keys are** (`proverif/capstone.pv`):
   176	- **Verified key.** It is the `kX` of `LayerAccepted(aid, lyr, t, ev, slot, kX, ppf, sg, fb)` (`:241-245`).
   177	  `AttestStage` checks `checksign(sgA, kA)` and then emits with `kX = kA` (`:618-619`; two-signer `:657-660`).
   178	  `slot` is `t`'s slot-A fingerprint `kfprA`.
   179	- **Under C-C15(i)** the verified key is `kEncW`, the wrapper key: `proverif/cap_cc15i_d.pv:707-708, :745-747`;
   180	  `cap_cc15i_a.pv:724-725, :763-765`.
   181	- **Standing key.** It is the `kT` of `EstablishedWrapped(aid, lyr, t, kT, core, ESTABLISHED)` (`:278-279`,
   182	  emitted `:844`). `kT = kX` (`:898`), where `kX` is the presented key from `stdMat` (`:877`), and
   183	  `core = attemptCore(=t, =ppfI, =sgI, _)` (`:884`).
   184	- Both paths take `aid`, `lyr`, `t` and keys from Front's one read (`:567-577`).
   185	
   186	**No event is needed, and the standing path is untouched.** The block below is inserted immediately before
   187	`(* ---- the REQUIRED retained queries`:
   188	```
   189	query aid: bitstring, lyr: bitstring, id: bitstring, kf: bitstring, ss: bitstring,
   190	      al: bitstring, vr: bitstring, kS: pkey, ppf: bitstring, sg: bitstring,
   191	      dcl: bitstring, ev: bitstring, kV: pkey, ppfV: bitstring, fb: bitstring;
   192	  event(EstablishedWrapped(aid, lyr, authTuple(id, kf, ss, al, vr), kS,
   193	          attemptCore(authTuple(id, kf, ss, al, vr), ppf, sg, dcl), ESTABLISHED))
   194	  && event(LayerAccepted(aid, lyr, authTuple(id, kf, ss, al, vr), ev, kf, kV, ppfV, sg, fb))
   195	  ==> kS = kV.
   196	```
   197	**The witness A8.4w** is the same premise with `kV` replaced by `kS` and no conclusion, as a reachability query.
   198	It must be REACHABLE. Its full text is in the script.
   199	
   200	**What the query joins on:** intake `aid`, layer `lyr`, tuple `t`, slot A (`slot = kf`) and the standing core's
   201	**signature term** `sg`. Together these pin the **innermost** acceptance. Standing establishes only at the
   202	innermost layer (BF-5, `:858-876`), and `sg = sgI` is an immutable join term (`PREDICTIONS.md:1005-1019`).
   203	
   204	**Rejected: the `ScopeKeyOnly` observer** (`:288`). It compares the scope **report**, which C-C15(ii)
   205	re-sources (`kEncW` on `scopeEnvelope`) while still verifying under `kA`.
   206	
   207	**Derived files.** `proverif/a84/a84_<src>.pv` is the source with one header comment prepended, every query
   208	replaced by a comment (`slice.py`'s regex), and the block inserted. Nothing else changes, and the sources are
   209	untouched.
   210	- The script is `proverif/dev/prereg_scratch/derive_a84.py`, sha256
   211	  `de35439b35889f1475afef012b968f03e3f90cdd2b7cc4c4b9ddad3b5af92b6d`. Its block text is the registered text.
   212	- The files were parsed and type-checked with the main process replaced by `0`, which is not a model run
   213	  (`…/prereg_scratch/parsecheck/`).
