   286	## 8. What would falsify the registration
   287	
   288	- **A predicted red that is not shown on both registered slices** is reported as **not shown** for that member,
   289	  never as green or as evidence against the guarantee. For (T) and (H), "not shown" includes a red whose half is
   290	  not visible in the trace.
   291	  - If **no** registered set-(1) member of a companion is shown, composed degraded severing evidence remains
   292	    **withheld**. The existing family evidence is reported separately, and any proposed narrowing of §A3.3 is
   293	    routed to the author for an explicit amendment. Nothing here narrows §A3.3 automatically.
   294	  - If only some members are shown, the read note lists the **shown** and the **unshown** members, and does not
   295	    imply complete companion discharge.
   296	- **Any red in a green-predicted control is a defect, and it stops the batch.** By trace inclusion it would be a
